{
  "_readme": [
    "Ground truth for scoring candidate NBA data sources.",
    "",
    "A career is the franchises a player ACTUALLY APPEARED FOR, in order, named as",
    "the franchise was called at the time. Consecutive seasons at one club are one",
    "entry; a later return is a separate entry, because that repetition is the",
    "puzzle.",
    "",
    "Appearances, not affiliation. Wikipedia infoboxes list teams a player was ON,",
    "which is not the same thing -- Barbosa was traded to Washington while injured",
    "and never played a game, so Washington is correctly absent from his career.",
    "You cannot ask someone to name a team a player never played for.",
    "",
    "Era names matter and are where sources go wrong: Seattle SuperSonics not",
    "Oklahoma City, Washington Bullets before 1997, Charlotte Bobcats between 2004",
    "and 2014.",
    "",
    "Verified 2026-09-04 against Wikipedia career infoboxes, cross-checked for",
    "appearances where a trade looked like it may not have involved any games."
  ],
